  m_Name: 2 - Movement
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: UtilityScriptIWrite::HintSO
  hintId: tutorial_movement
  isUnlockedByDefault: 1
  ignoreLock: 0
  title: Movement
  image: {fileID: 0}
  description: "Movement commands are used to control the robot\u2019s position and
    direction during exploration.\n\nAvailable movement commands:\n<font=\"JetBrainsMono
    SDF\"><color=#33CC66>move_forward</color>()</font> \u2192 Move one tile forward\n<font=\"JetBrainsMono
    SDF\"><color=#33CC66>move_backward</color>()</font> \u2192 Move one tile backward\n<font=\"JetBrainsMono
    SDF\"><color=#33CC66>turn_right</color>()</font> \u2192 Rotate the robot to the
    right\n<font=\"JetBrainsMono SDF\"><color=#33CC66>turn_left</color>()</font>
    \u2192 Rotate the robot to the left\n<font=\"JetBrainsMono SDF\"><color=#33CC66>wait</color>()</font>
    \u2192 Do nothing for one turn\n\nMost objects and interactions require proper
    positioning, so careful movement is important while exploring dangerous areas."
  isImageBig: 0
